#
# Tomcat OpenSSL QUIC endpoint: work-gated poll subset (Phase C)
# ==============================================================
#
# Applies on top of the OpenSSL patches:
#   openssl-quic-work-gated-port-tick.patch   (Phase A)
#   openssl-quic-poll-ready-channels.patch    (Phase B)
#
# Problem
# -------
# The endpoint passed every listener, established connection and registered
# stream to SSL_poll() on every ticked iteration. With an idle fleet this made
# each keepalive datagram cost one per-item readout over all connections, even
# after the libssl engine tick and poll readout were work-gated. Stream items
# for the three server-initiated HTTP/3 control/QPACK streams also kept an O(3N)
# stream-item scan on the idle path.
#
# What it does
# ------------
# 1. Binds the optional SSL_get_quic_ready_channels() symbol. The symbol is not
#    part of the required QUIC_AVAILABLE set; a build without it uses the old
#    all-items poll path.
# 2. Adds a compact per-iteration poll subset to QuicPollSet:
#      beginPoll(), addPollItem(), addAllPollItems()
#      writePollItems(), syncPollRevents()
#    Only the selected items are written into the native SSL_POLL_ITEM array
#    and only their revents are read back. The subset selection survives a
#    poll-set shrink while a readout is in flight.
# 3. Builds the endpoint subset from:
#      - the listener item, always;
#      - connections returned by SSL_get_quic_ready_channels();
#      - the registered stream items of those connections;
#      - bidirectional request streams with a socket wrapper, whose application
#        read/write interest can persist without new parent-connection activity.
#    Idle connections are no longer polled on every iteration.
# 4. Tracks registered stream poll items so they are removed from the subset on
#    normal close, poll failure and connection teardown.
# 5. Gives newly registered or ready-connection-touched stream items a bounded
#    four-pass linger. This covers buffered data which becomes readable one
#    pass after the parent connection's ready entry was drained. Read/error
#    events refresh the linger; write-only W events do not, so quiescent
#    server unidirectional streams do not stay polled forever.
#
# No public Tomcat configuration change is introduced. The compatibility path
# for older OpenSSL builds keeps the previous all-items behaviour.
#
# Files
# -----
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/LocalStrings.properties
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/QuicBindings.java
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/QuicConnectionWrapper.java
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/QuicOpenSSLEndpoint.java
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/QuicPollItem.java
#   java/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/QuicPollSet.java
#   test/org/apache/tomcat/util/net/quic/openssl/TestQuicPollSet.java
#
# Validation
# ----------
#   TestQuicPollSet: 6 tests, 0 failures
#   Full Tomcat HTTP/3 suite: 588 run, 0 errors, 2 skipped. Under the shared
#     host's load the only failure observed across repeated runs was the
#     TestAsyncFlush 10 s aioquic timeout, which passes 10/10 in isolation and
#     is documented upstream as non-release-blocking.
#
# Measured (same shared host; 12 s load window, 40 s idle sample)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#   idle4000 keepalive:   32.25 % (report baseline) -> 2.0-2.15 % poller
#   idle8000 keepalive:   81 %+ (report baseline) -> 2.27-2.45 % poller
#   8x25 load:            92,716-93,483 rps, p50 2.58-2.59 ms,
#                         p99 4.94-4.99 ms, 10.1-10.2 us/req,
#                         poller 94.16-94.41 %, 0 errors
#   mixed 1x32 + 2000:    18,280 rps, p50 2.09 ms, p99 4.01 ms,
#                         15.7 us/req, 0 load errors
#
# Apply from the Tomcat source root with:
#   git apply /path/to/tomcat-openssl-quic-ready-poll.patch
# or:
#   patch -p1 < /path/to/tomcat-openssl-quic-ready-poll.patch
#
# Generated against Tomcat HEAD 63344d8953 (2026-11-20).
#
